  "question": {
    "text": "Let [.] denote the greatest integer function. If $\\int_0^{e^3}\\left[\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{x}-1}}\\right] \\mathrm{dx}=\\alpha-\\log _{\\mathrm{e}} 2$, then $\\alpha^3$ is equal to _______ .",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$f(x)=\\frac{1}{e^{x-1}}=e^{1-x}$<br/>\\begin{array}{c|c}\\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})=2 & \\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})=1 \\\\\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{x}-1}}=2 & \\mathrm{x}=1 \\\\\\mathrm{x}=1-\\ln 2 &\\end{array}<br/>$f(0)=e^1=2.71$<br/>$f\\left(e^3\\right)=e^{1-e^3} \\in(0,1)$<br/>$\\mathrm{I}=\\int_0^{1-\\ell \\mathrm{n} 2} 2 \\mathrm{dx}+\\int_{1-\\ell \\mathrm{n} 2}^1 1 \\mathrm{dx}+\\int_1^{\\mathrm{e}^3} 0 \\mathrm{dx}$<br/>$=2(1-\\ell \\operatorname{n} 2-0)+1(1-1+\\ln 2)+0$<br/>$\\alpha-\\ln 2=2-\\ln 2$<br/>$\\alpha=2$<br/>$\\alpha^3=8$",
    "image": null
  },
